endorp, Rudi G J","name_org":"Westendorp, Rudi G.J.","orcid":"0000-0002-0672-8372","rank":74,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"67","first":"Alessandra","key":"zonaripau","last":"Zonari","name":"Zonari, Alessandra","rank":75,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Daniela","key":"bakulapau","last":"Bakula","locid":"e9dae8c1-e9e5-4f57-813c-1c4c6d2d4cc3","name":"Bakula, Daniela","rank":76,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"54","corresponding":null,"first":"Alex","key":"zhavoronkovpau","last":"Zhavoronkov","name":"Zhavoronkov, Alex","rank":77,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"scheibyeknudsenpau","last":"Scheibye-Knudsen","locid":"161fd11a-45bf-427a-8307-f111b06510bb","name":"Scheibye-Knudsen, Morten","rank":78,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35089871"],"pub":{"doi":"10.18632/aging.203859","issn":["19454589"],"issue":"2","journal":"Aging","pages":"532-543","publisher":"Impact Journals LLC","status":"p","title":"Aging","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85124173756"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8d44a138-497e-40bf-808d-db6372fbd887","ku-42a62724-fd9f-4c0b-88b2-3132bae110b0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Meeting Report : Aging Research and Drug Discovery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.61-022955","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Serum insulin-like growth factor 1 (sIGF-1) is an important growth factor in childhood. However, studies on sIGF-1 among children from low-income countries are few, and the role of body composition is unknown. Objectives: To assess the associations of anthropometry, body composition, inflammation, and breastfeeding with sIGF-1 among children with moderate acute malnutrition (MAM). Methods: A cross-sectional study based on admission data from 6- to 23-mo-old children with MAM participating in a nutrition intervention trial (Treatfood) in Burkina Faso. Linear regression analysis was used to identify correlates of sIGF-1. Results: Among 1546 children, the median (IQR) sIGF-1 was 12 (8.2-18.3) ng/mL. sIGF-1 was highest at 6 mo, with a nadir ∼10-11 mo, and higher in girls than boys. Length-for-age z score (LAZ), weight-for-length z score (WLZ), and midupper arm circumference were positively associated with sIGF-1 (P ≤ 0.001). Fat-free mass (FFM) was also positively associated, as sIGF-1 increased 1.5 (95% CI: 0.5, 2.5) ng/mL for each 1-kg increase in FFM. However, the association disappeared after adjustment for height. Elevated serum C-reactive protein and α1-acid glycoprotein were negatively associated with sIGF-1 (P ≤ 0.001), as was fever (P < 0.001) but not a positive malaria test per se (P = 0.15). Children never breastfed had lower sIGF-1 (-5.1; 95% CI: -9.8, -0.3). Conclusions: LAZ and WLZ were positively and inflammation negatively associated with sIGF-1. As all children were moderately malnourished and many had inflammation, this probably explains the very low median sIGF-1. The association of FFM with sIGF-1 was fully explained by height. There was a marked age pattern, with a nadir in late infancy, confirming findings from smaller studies from well-nourished populations. There is a need for prospective studies to disentangle the role of sIGF-1 in growth and health.  This trial was registered at https://www.isrctn.com as ISRCTN42569496.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Kjær, Thora Wesenberg","Grenov, Benedikte","Yaméogo, Charles W","Fabiansen, Christian","Iuel-Brockdorff, Ann-Sophie Julie D","Cichon, Bernardette","Nielsen, Nick Schou","Filteau, Suzanne","Briend, André","Wells, Jonathan C K","Michaelsen, Kim F.","Friis, Henrik","Faurholt-Jepsen, Daniel","Christensen, Vibeke Brix"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-476511"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Burkina Faso","Finland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine","Tampere University","University College London","Université de Ouagadougou"],"keyword":["Body composition","Faculty of Science","Inflammation","Insulin like growth factor 1 IGF 1","Low income country","Moderate acute malnutrition"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Læger Uden Grænser, København"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"correlates of serum igf 000000000001 in young children with moderate acute malnutrition a cross sectional study in burkina faso","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/313871070/Pre_print_Correlates_of_serum_IGF_1_in_young_children_with_moderate_acute_malnutrition_a_cross_sectional_study_in_Burkina_Faso.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-476511","identifier":[{"id":"33963730","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85116958043","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8af2ada6-f8a7-4d36-bc9c-fc13330f39e3"],"keyword":["Body composition","Faculty of Science","Inflammation","Insulin-like growth factor 1 (IGF-1)","Low-income country","Moderate