{"author_count":11,"contributors":["Nygård, Mari","Hansen, Bo T.","Kjaer, Susanne K.","Hortlund, Maria","Tryggvadóttir, Laufey","Munk, Christian","Lagheden, Camilla","Sigurdardottir, Lara G.","Campbell, Suzanne","Liaw, Kai-li","Dillner, Joakim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-516800"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"human papillomavirus genotype specific risks for cervical intraepithelial lesions","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/21645515.2020.1814097","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-516800","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8018444","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32990181","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85091686202","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ce7a1320-68fd-4ff4-8bef-1aae379edc36"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3E98F09D16077E508ACF6661C4DB42E4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/21645515.2020.1814097","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/279629797/Human_papillomavirus_genotype_specific_risks_for_cervical_intraepithelial_lesions.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Mari","key":"nygårdpau","last":"Nygård","name":"Nygård, Mari","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bo T.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Bo T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne K.","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maria","key":"hortlundpau","last":"Hortlund","name":"Hortlund, Maria","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Laufey","key":"tryggvadóttirpau","last":"Tryggvadóttir","name":"Tryggvadóttir, Laufey","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"munkpau","last":"Munk","name":"Munk, Christian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Camilla","key":"laghedenpau","last":"Lagheden","name":"Lagheden, Camilla","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lara G.","key":"sigurdardottirpau","last":"Sigurdardottir","name":"Sigurdardottir, Lara G.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Suzanne","key":"campbellpau","last":"Campbell","name":"Campbell, Suzanne","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kai-li","key":"liawpau","last":"Liaw","name":"Liaw, Kai-li","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Joakim","key":"dillnerpau","last":"Dillner","name":"Dillner, Joakim","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32990181"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/21645515.2020.1814097","issn":["15548619","21645515"],"issn_org":["21645515"],"issue":"4","journal":"Human Vaccines & Immunotherapeutics","pages":"972-981","status":"p","title":"Human Vaccines & Immunotherapeutics","title_org":"Human vaccines & immunotherapeutics","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091686202"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ce7a1320-68fd-4ff4-8bef-1aae379edc36"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Human papillomavirus genotype-specific risks for cervical intraepithelial lesions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-516800","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: In 2009, both Norway and Denmark initiated routine quadrivalent human papillomavirus vaccination (qHPV) for 12-year-old girls; however, Denmark also introduced free-of-charge multi-cohort vaccination for older age groups in 2008. We aim to describe trends in genital warts (GWs) incidence rates (IRs) among men and women and qHPV vaccine coverage among women in Norway and Denmark in 2006–2015. Methods: We linked multiple national health registries in Norway and Denmark via national personal identifiers to access data on GWs incidence and qHPV vaccination among women and men aged 12–35 years residing in Norway and Denmark in 2006–2015. We calculated age-specific and age-standardized GWs IRs, GWs IR trends before (2006–2009) and after (2009–2015) the implementation of qHPV vaccination, and qHPV vaccine coverage among women. Results: In Norway and Denmark together, there were more than 200,000 cases of incident GWs and over 710,000 girls got at least one dose of qHPV vaccine during the study period. The total qHPV coverage in Norway and Denmark in 2015 was among women aged 12–35 years 24% and 70%, respectively. GWs IRs in Norway and Denmark decreased annually in 2009–2015 among women by 4.8% (95% confidence interval: 4.3 to 5.3) and 18.0% (95%CI: 17.5 to 18.6), respectively, and among men 1.9% (95%CI: 1.4 to 2.4) and 10.7% (95%CI: 10.3 to 11.2), respectively. In Denmark, GWs IRs decreased rapidly among both sexes and all age groups after qHPV vaccination, while Norway showed only a modest decrease. Conclusion: Rapid decline in HPV-related morbidity is feasible with high coverage of multi-cohort vaccination. However, the decision to vaccinate a single cohort of 12-years-old girls only will postpone HPV-related disease control by at least a decade. Thus countries planning HPV vaccination programs should also initiate multi-cohort vaccination for faster disease control.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Orumaa, Madleen","Kjaer, Susanne K.","Dehlendorff, Christian","Munk, Christian","Olsen, Anne Olaug","Hansen, Bo T.","Campbell, Suzanne","Nygård, Mari"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-395118"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Condylomata Acuminata","Papillomavirus Infections prevention control","Real world data"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of hpv multi cohort vaccination real world evidence of faster control of hpv related morbidity","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.vaccine.2019.12.016","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-395118","identifier":[{"id":"31917039","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85078440168","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-02bb82a5-1a55-44b6-b095-cab7785b9cd5"],"keyword":["Condylomata Acuminata","Human Papillomavirus Recombinant Vaccine Quadrivalent","Immunization Program","Multi-cohort vaccination","Papillomavirus Infections/prevention & control","Real-world data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AC88FD76D96E511A28A9104B8B8DB02B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.vaccine.2019.12.016","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/261000141/1_s2.0_S0264410X19316585_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Madleen","key":"orumaapau","last":"Orumaa","name":"Orumaa, Madleen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne K.","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christian","key":"dehlendorffpau","last":"Dehlendorff","name":"Dehlendorff, Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"munkpau","last":"Munk","name":"Munk, Christian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne Olaug","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Anne Olaug","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bo T.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Bo T.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Suzanne","key":"campbellpau","last":"Campbell","name":"Campbell, Suzanne","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mari","key":"nygårdpau","last":"Nygård","name":"Nygård, Mari","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31917039"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.vaccine.2019.12.016","issn":["0264410X","13552732"],"issn_org":["0264410X"],"issue":"6","journal":"Vaccine","pages":"1345-1351","status":"p","title":"Vaccine","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078440168"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-02bb82a5-1a55-44b6-b095-cab7785b9cd5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The impact of HPV multi-cohort vaccination : Real-world evidence of faster control of HPV-related morbidity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-395118","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Post-marketing studies are commonly performed to follow-up on the safety and effectiveness of a drug or vaccine after approval has been obtained. These post-marketing studies may involve the collection of real-world data from registries and clinical biobanks in order to obtain real-world evidence. As this approach can monitor the effects of pharmaceutical products over decades, it is particularly necessary for the development of safe and effective vaccines. A long-term follow-up (LTFU) study was initiated as an extension of a phase 3 clinical study (V501–015; NCT00092534) to assess the effectiveness, immunogenicity and safety of the quadrivalent human papillomavirus (qHPV) vaccine for up to 14 years after the start of vaccination. The LTFU study included participants from Denmark, Iceland, Norway, and Sweden, and assessed qHPV vaccine effectiveness against cervical pre-cancers and cancers caused by the oncogenic HPV types 16 and 18. In particular, our study utilized Nordic national health registries, in which individual patient records were linked by a unique Personal Identity Number. Here, we describe the overall implementation and methodology of the qHPV vaccine LTFU study conducted in the Nordic region. The LTFU study format we describe here supported a comprehensive follow-up process, with near-complete retrieval of registry data and specimens from local laboratories achieved in a timely manner; therefore, we have demonstrated that such a collection is feasible and can be used to address stringent post-marketing requirements.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Enerly, Espen","Berger, Sophie","Kjaer, Susanne K.","Sundström, Karin","Campbell, Suzanne","Tryggvadóttir, Laufey","Munk, Christian","Hortlund, Maria","Joshi, Amita","Saah, Alfred J.","Nygård, Mari"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-471030"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Long term follow up","Real world data","Real world evidence"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of real world data for hpv vaccine trial follow up in the nordic region","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-471030","identifier":[{"id":"32247041","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85083360827","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-81a4bd3d-8ed1-4a95-baea-ae5146627805"],"keyword":["Long-term follow-up","Post-marketing requirements","Public health registries","Quadrivalent human papillomavirus vaccine","Real-world data","Real-world evidence"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E242BEBACE50D123786375104666EE79"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Espen","key":"enerlypau","last":"Enerly","name":"Enerly, Espen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sophie","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","name":"Berger, Sophie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne K.","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","name_org":"Kjær, Susanne K.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Karin","key":"sundströmpau","last":"Sundström","name":"Sundström, Karin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Suzanne","key":"campbellpau","last":"Campbell","name":"Campbell, Suzanne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Laufey","key":"tryggvadóttirpau","last":"Tryggvadóttir","name":"Tryggvadóttir, Laufey","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"munkpau","last":"Munk","name":"Munk, Christian","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maria","key":"hortlundpau","last":"Hortlund","name":"Hortlund, Maria","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Amita","key":"joshipau","last":"Joshi","name":"Joshi, Amita","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alfred J.","key":"saahpau","last":"Saah","name":"Saah, Alfred J.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mari","key":"nygårdpau","last":"Nygård","name":"Nygård, Mari","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32247041"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cct.2020.105996","issn":["15517144","15592030"],"issn_org":["15517144"],"journal":"Contemporary Clinical Trials","paperid":"105996","status":"p","title":"Contemporary Clinical Trials","volume":"92"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083360827"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-81a4bd3d-8ed1-4a95-baea-ae5146627805"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Use of real-world data for HPV vaccine trial follow-up in the Nordic region","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-471030","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: The natural history of human papillomavirus (HPV) infection has been studied extensively in young women; this study investigated HPV infection in adult women. Methods: Data from 3817 women aged 24–45 years in a global trial of the 4-valent HPV (6/11/16/18) vaccine were used to calculate prevalence of anogenital infections containing 9-valent (9v) HPV vaccine types (6/11/16/18/31/33/45/52/58) and five non-vaccine types (35/39/51/56/59). Incidence of infections and persistent infections was estimated for 989 placebo recipients naive to all 14 HPV types at baseline. Age-adjusted hazard ratios were calculated for various sociodemographic factors. Results: Prevalence of anogenital infection was highest in France at 29.2% (9vHPV types) and 21.7% (non-vaccine types) and lowest in the Philippines at 7.6% (9vHPV types) and 5.1% (non-vaccine types). Overall, HPV incidence (per 100 person-years) was 5.2 (9vHPV types) and 4.7 (non-vaccine types), and incidence of persistent infection was 2.7 (9vHPV types) and 2.1 (non-vaccine types). Factors associated with new HPV infections included younger age, younger age at first intercourse, being single, current use of tobacco, and higher number of past and recent sex partners. Conclusions: Because mid-adult women acquire new HPV infections, administration of the 9vHPV vaccine could reduce HPV-related morbidity and mortality in this population.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Ferris, Daron G.","Brown, Darron R.","Giuliano, Anna R.","Myers, Evan","Joura, Elmar A.","Garland, Suzanne M.","Kjaer, Susanne K.","Perez, Gonzalo","Saah, Alfred","Luxembourg, Alain","Velicer, Christine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-452464"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["HPV vaccine","Human papillomavirus","Incidence","Persistent infection","Risk factor"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence incidence and natural history of hpv infection in adult women ages 000000000024 to 000000000045 participating in a vaccine trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pvr.2020.100202","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-452464","identifier":[{"id":"85089274641","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7453107","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32464334","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-62b36255-6937-40bf-9496-3916af360f0d"],"keyword":["Adult women","HPV vaccine","Human papillomavirus","Incidence","Persistent infection","Risk factor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-563398B03AAFC6575969AE2EA59E02FE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/260990962/1_s2.0_S1053811920308491_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pvr.2020.100202","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Daron G.","key":"ferrispau","last":"Ferris","name":"Ferris, Daron G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Darron R.","key":"brownpau","last":"Brown","name":"Brown, Darron R.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna R.","key":"giulianopau","last":"Giuliano","name":"Giuliano, Anna R.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Evan","key":"myerspau","last":"Myers","name":"Myers, Evan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elmar A.","key":"jourapau","last":"Joura","name":"Joura, Elmar A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Suzanne M.","key":"garlandpau","last":"Garland","name":"Garland, Suzanne M.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne K.","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gonzalo","key":"perezpau","last":"Perez","name":"Perez, Gonzalo","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alfred","key":"saahpau","last":"Saah","name":"Saah, Alfred","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alain","key":"luxembourgpau","last":"Luxembourg","name":"Luxembourg, Alain","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christine","key":"velicerpau","last":"Velicer","name":"Velicer, Christine","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32464334"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.pvr.2020.100202","issn":["24058521"],"journal":"Papillomavirus Research","paperid":"100202","status":"p","title":"Papillomavirus Research","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089274641"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-62b36255-6937-40bf-9496-3916af360f0d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prevalence, incidence, and natural history of HPV infection in adult women ages 24 to 45 participating in a vaccine trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-452464","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Nine-valent human papillomavirus (9vHPV) vaccine efficacy against disease and cervical surgeries related to all nine vaccine components was assessed compared with a historic placebo population. This was not assessed in the 9vHPV vaccine efficacy trial since the trial was quadrivalent HPV (qHPV) vaccine-controlled, efficacy was measured for the five HPV types covered only by 9vHPV vaccine (HPV31/33/45/52/58), but not the four types covered by both vaccines (HPV6/11/16/18). Methods: Three international, randomized, double-blind studies were conducted using the same methodology. In the 9vHPV vaccine study (NCT00543543), 7106 and 7109 women received 9vHPV or qHPV vaccine, respectively. In the historic qHPV vaccine studies (FUTURE I [NCT00092521] and II [NCT00092534]), 8810 and 8812 women received qHPV vaccine or placebo, respectively, based on the same eligibility criteria. Cervical cytological testing was performed regularly. Biopsy or definitive therapy specimens were assessed for HPV DNA. Results: Among women negative for 14 HPV types prior to vaccination, incidence of high-grade cervical disease (9vHPV, n = 2 cases; placebo, n = 141 cases) and cervical surgery (9vHPV, n = 3 cases; placebo, n = 170 cases) related to the nine HPV types was reduced by 98.2% (95% confidence interval [CI], 93.6–99.7) and 97.8% (95% CI, 93.4–99.4), respectively. The 9vHPV vaccine did not prevent disease related to vaccine HPV types detected at baseline, but significantly reduced cervical, vulvar, and vaginal diseases related to other vaccine HPV types. Conclusions: Effective implementation of the 9vHPV vaccine may substantially reduce the burden of HPV-related diseases and related medical procedures. Trial registrations: clinicaltrials.gov: NCT00543543, NCT00092521, NCT00092534.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Giuliano, Anna R.","Joura, Elmar A.","Garland, Suzanne M.","Huh, Warner K.","Iversen, Ole Erik","Kjaer, Susanne K.","Ferenczy, Alex","Kurman, Robert J.","Ronnett, Brigitte M.","Stoler, Mark H.","Bautista, Oliver M.","Moeller, Erin","Ritter, Michael","Shields, Christine","Luxembourg, Alain"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-398960"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Austria","Canada","Norway","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Johns Hopkins University","McGill University","Medical University of Vienna","Merck","Murdoch Children's Research Institute","Royal Women's Hospital","University of Alabama at Birmingham","University of Bergen","University of Melbourne","University of South Florida","University of Virginia"],"keyword":["Cervical cancer","Cervical intraepithelial neoplasia CIN","HPV","Persistent infection","Vaccine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nine valent hpv vaccine efficacy against related diseases and definitive therapy comparison with historic placebo population","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ygyno.2019.03.253","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-398960","identifier":[{"id":"85064037417","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30982556","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-092c0b5d-1b63-4be1-b572-03f77daea1f6"],"keyword":["Cervical cancer","Cervical intraepithelial neoplasia (CIN)","HPV","Persistent infection","Vaccine","Vulvar intraepithelial neoplasia (VIN)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BD08F0459702D010A8DA0B5C2AB1FFBD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/1