{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) have been associated with improved survival in some cancers, but evidence for ovarian cancer is limited. METHODS: Pooling individual-level data from 12 Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium studies, we evaluated the association between self-reported, pre-diagnosis use of common analgesics and overall/progression-free/disease-specific survival among 7694 women with invasive epithelial ovarian cancer (4273 deaths). RESULTS: Regular analgesic use (at least once per week) was not associated with overall survival (pooled hazard ratios, pHRs (95% confidence intervals): aspirin 0.96 (0.88-1.04); non-aspirin NSAIDs 0.97 (0.89-1.05); acetaminophen 1.01 (0.93-1.10)), nor with progression-free/disease-specific survival. There was however a survival advantage for users of any NSAIDs in studies clearly defining non-use as less than once per week (pHR=0.89 (0.82-0.98)). CONCLUSIONS: Although this study did not show a clear association between analgesic use and ovarian cancer survival, further investigation with clearer definitions of use and information about post-diagnosis use is warranted.","author_count":35,"contributors":["Dixon, Suzanne C","Nagle, Christina M","Wentzensen, Nicolas","Trabert, Britton","Beeghly-Fadiel, Alicia","Schildkraut, Joellen M","Moysich, Kirsten B","deFazio, Anna","Risch, Harvey A","Rossing, Mary Anne","Doherty, Jennifer A","Wicklund, Kristine G","Goodman, Marc T","Modugno, Francesmary","Ness, Roberta B","Edwards, Robert P","Jensen, Allan","Kjaer, Susanne K.","Høgdall, Estrid","Berchuck, Andrew","Cramer, Daniel W","Terry, Kathryn L","Poole, Elizabeth M","Bandera, Elisa V","Paddock, Lisa E","Anton-Culver, Hoda","Ziogas, Argyrios","Menon, Usha","Gayther, Simon A","Ramus, Susan J","Gentry-Maharaj, Aleksandra","Pearce, Celeste Leigh","Wu, Anna H","Pike, Malcolm C","Webb, Penelope M"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-448744"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["Australian Ovarian Cancer Study Group"],"keyword":["Acetaminophen therapeutic use","Adult","Aged","Analgesics therapeutic use","Anti Inflammatory Agents Non Steroidal therapeutic use","Aspirin therapeutic use","Disease Free Survival","Female","Humans","Middle Aged","Ovarian Neoplasms drug therapy","Proportional Hazards Models","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of common analgesic medications and ovarian cancer survival results from a pooled analysis in the ovarian cancer association consortium","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/bjc.2017.68","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-448744","identifier":[{"id":"28350790","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85016433040","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5418444","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-5c5e7817-a8bc-482d-9c21-9f222d1555bf"],"keyword":["Acetaminophen/therapeutic use","Adult","Aged","Analgesics/therapeutic use","Anti-Inflammatory Agents, Non-Steroidal/therapeutic use","Anticarcinogenic Agents/therapeutic use","Aspirin/therapeutic use","Disease-Free Survival","Female","Humans","Middle Aged","Ovarian Neoplasms/drug therapy","Proportional Hazards Models","Risk Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-293BB44CF32BA850335015CB27933EBE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/bjc.2017.68","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/197763378/bjc201768.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno