ersity of Copenhagen"],"title":"Assessing the genetic architecture of epithelial ovarian cancer histological subtypes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-532027","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Background: We estimated the proportion of cervical intraepithelial neoplasia (CIN) cases attributed to 14 HPV types, including quadrivalent (qHPV) (6/11/16/18) and 9-valent (9vHPV) (6/11/16/18/31/33/45/52/58) vaccine types, by region. Methods: Women ages 15-26 and 24-45 years from 5 regions were enrolled in qHPV vaccine clinical trials. Among 10,706 women (placebo arms), 1539 CIN1, 945 CIN2/3, and 24 adenocarcinoma in situ (AIS) cases were diagnosed by pathology panel consensus. Results: Predominant HPV types were 16/51/52/56 (anogenital infection), 16/39/51/52/56 (CIN1), and 16/31/52/58 (CIN2/3). In regions with largest sample sizes, minimal regional variation was observed in 9vHPV type prevalence in CIN1 (~50%) and CIN2/3 (81-85%). Types 31/33/45/52/58 accounted for 25-30% of CIN1 in Latin America and Europe, but 14-18% in North America and Asia. Types 31/33/45/52/58 accounted for 33-38% of CIN2/3 in Latin America (younger women), Europe, and Asia, but 17-18% of CIN2/3 in Latin America (older women) and North America. Non-vaccine HPV types 35/39/51/56/59 had similar or higher prevalence than qHPV types in CIN1 and were attributed to 2-11% of CIN2/3. Conclusions: The 9vHPV vaccine could potentially prevent the majority of CIN1-3, irrespective of geographic region. Notwithstanding, non-vaccine types 35/39/51/56/59 may still be responsible for some CIN1, and to a lesser extent CIN2/3.","author_count":26,"contributors":["Castellsagué, Xavier","Ault, Kevin A","Bosch, F Xavier","Brown, Darron R","Cuzick, Jack","Ferris, Daron G","Joura, Elmar A","Garland, Suzanne M","Giuliano, Anna R.","Hernandez-Avila, Mauricio","Huh, Warner","Iversen, Ole-Erik","Kjaer, Susanne K.","Luna, Joaquin","Monsonego, Joseph","Muñoz, Nubia","Myers, Evan R","Paavonen, Jorma","Pitisuttihum, Punnee","Steben, Marc","Wheeler, Cosette M","Perez, Gonzalo","Saah, Alfred","Luxembourg, Alain","Sings, Heather L","Velicer, Christine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-444915"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, Central","America, North","America, South","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Austria","Colombia","Finland","France","Mexico","Norway","Spain","Thailand","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Augusta University","Bellvitge Biomedical Research Institute","Duke University","Fundacion Universitaria Sanitas","Indiana University-Purdue University Columbus","Institut du Col","Instituto Nacional de Salud Publica","Mahidol University","Medical University of Vienna","Merck","Murdoch Children's Research Institute","National Institute of Cancer","Queen Mary University of London","Universidad del Rosario","University of Alabama","University of Bergen","University of Helsinki","University of Kansas","University of New Mexico","University of South Florida"],"keyword":["Adenocarcinoma in Situ","Cervical Intraepithelial Neoplasia","Cervical cancer","Human papillomavirus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"human papillomavirus detection in cervical neoplasia attributed to 000000000012 high risk human papillomavirus genotypes by region","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pvr.2016.03.002","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-444915","identifier":[{"id":"29074187","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84961675401","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-56285e83-7633-43eb-b841-479f2609e1b3"],"keyword":["Adenocarcinoma in situ","Cervical cancer","Cervical intraepithelial neoplasia","Human papillomavirus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8F7516434150442