suttihum","name":"Pitisuttihum, Punnee","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marc","key":"stebenpau","last":"Steben","name":"Steben, Marc","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"19","first":"Cosette M","key":"wheelerpau","last":"Wheeler","name":"Wheeler, Cosette M","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"20 21","first":"Gonzalo","key":"perezpau","last":"Perez","name":"Perez, Gonzalo","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"20","first":"Alfred","key":"saahpau","last":"Saah","name":"Saah, Alfred","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"20","first":"Alain","key":"luxembourgpau","last":"Luxembourg","name":"Luxembourg, Alain","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"20","first":"Heather L","key":"singspau","last":"Sings","name":"Sings, Heather L","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"20","first":"Christine","key":"velicerpau","last":"Velicer","name":"Velicer, Christine","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29074187"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.pvr.2016.03.002","issn":["24058521"],"journal":"Papillomavirus Research","pages":"61-69","status":"p","title":"Papillomavirus Research","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84961675401"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-56285e83-7633-43eb-b841-479f2609e1b3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Human papillomavirus detection in cervical neoplasia attributed to 12 high-risk human papillomavirus genotypes by region","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-444915","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: The overall safety profile of the 9-valent human papillomavirus (9vHPV) vaccine was evaluated across 7 Phase III studies, conducted in males and females (nonpregnant at entry), 9 to 26 years of age. METHODS: Vaccination was administered as a 3-dose regimen at day 1, and months 2 and 6. More than 15 000 subjects received ≥1 dose of 9vHPV vaccine. In 2 of the studies, >7000 control subjects received ≥1 dose of quadrivalent HPV (qHPV) vaccine. Serious and nonserious adverse events (AEs) and new medical conditions were recorded throughout the study. Subjects testing positive for pregnancy at day 1 were not vaccinated; those who became pregnant after day 1 were discontinued from further vaccination until resolution of the pregnancy. Pregnancies detected after study start (n = 2950) were followed to outcome. RESULTS: The most common AEs (≥5%) experienced by 9vHPV vaccine recipients were injection-site AEs (pain, swelling, erythema) and vaccine-related systemic AEs (headache, pyrexia). Injection-site AEs were more common in 9vHPV vaccine than qHPV vaccine recipients; most were mild-to-moderate in intensity. Discontinuations and vaccine-related serious AEs were rare (0.1% and <0.1%, respectively). Seven deaths were reported; none were considered vaccine related. The proportions of pregnancies with adverse outcome were within ranges reported in the general population. CONCLUSIONS: The 9vHPV vaccine was generally well tolerated in subjects aged 9 to 26 years with an AE profile similar to that of the qHPV vaccine; injection-site AEs were more common with 9vHPV vaccine. Its additional coverage and safety profile support widespread 9vHPV vaccination.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Moreira, Edson D","Block, Stan L","Ferris, Daron G","Giuliano, Anna R.","Iversen, Ole-Erik","Joura, Elmar A","Kosalaraksa, Pope","Schilling, Andrea","Van Damme, Pierre","Bornstein, Jacob","Bosch, F Xavier","Pils, Sophie","Cuzick, Jack","Garland, Suzanne M","Huh, Warner","Kjaer, Susanne K.","Qi, Hong","Hyatt, Donna","Martin, Jason","Moeller, Erin","Ritter, Michael","Baudin, Martine","Luxembourg, Alain"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-516052"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"safety profile of the 000000000009 valent hpv vaccine a combined analysis of 000000000007 phase iii clinical trials","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-516052","identifier":[{"id":"84982855434","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27422279","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-cd4e6166-beb2-4c66-816a-beabb70c55b8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-873265F8AC2DFCE0482DCBCE97FBDC1E"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Edson D","key":"moreirapau","last":"Moreira","name":"Moreira, Edson D","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stan L","key":"blockpau","last":"Block","name":"Block, Stan L","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Daron G","key":"ferrispau","last":"Ferris","name":"Ferris, Daron G","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna R.","key":"giulianopau","last":"Giuliano","name":"Giuliano, Anna R.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ole-Erik","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","name":"Iversen, Ole-Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elmar A","key":"jourapau","last":"Joura","name":"Joura, Elmar A","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pope","key":"kosalaraksapau","last":"Kosalaraksa","name":"Kosalaraksa, Pope","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrea","key":"schillingpau","last":"Schilling","name":"Schilling, Andrea","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pierre","key":"vandammepau","last":"Van Damme","name":"Van Damme, Pierre","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob","key":"bornsteinpau","last":"Bornstein","name":"Bornstein, Jacob","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"F Xavier","key":"boschpau","last":"Bosch","name":"Bosch, F Xavier","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sophie","key":"pilspau","last":"Pils","name":"Pils, Sophie","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jack","key":"cuzickpau","last":"Cuzick","name":"Cuzick, Jack","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Suzanne M","key":"garlandpau","last":"Garland","name":"Garland, Suzanne M","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Warner","key":"huhpau","last":"Huh","name":"Huh, Warner","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne K.","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hong","key":"qipau","last":"Qi","name":"Qi, Hong","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Donna","key":"hyattpau","last":"Hyatt","name":"Hyatt, Donna","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jason","key":"martinpau","last":"Martin","name":"Martin, Jason","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erin","key":"moellerpau","last":"Moeller","name":"Moeller, Erin","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"ritterpau","last":"Ritter","name":"Ritter, Michael","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Martine","key":"baudinpau","last":"Baudin","name":"Baudin, Martine","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alain","key":"luxembourgpau","last":"Luxembourg","name":"Luxembourg, Alain","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27422279"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1542/peds.2015-4387","issn":["00314005","10984275"],"issn_org":["00314005"],"issue":"2","journal":"Pediatrics","paperid":"e20154387","status":"p","title":"Pediatrics","volume":"138"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84982855434"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cd4e6166-beb2-4c66-816a-beabb70c55b8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Safety profile of the 9-valent HPV vaccine : A combined analysis of 7 phase III clinical trials","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-516052","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: A quadrivalent human papillomavirus (HPV4) type 6/11/16/18 vaccine (GARDASIL/SILGARD®) has been licensed in many countries around the world for the prevention of cervical, vulvar, vaginal, and anal cancers and precancers, as well as external genital warts causally related to HPV types 6/11/16/18. Across 7 phase 3 clinical trials involving more than 29,000 males and females ages 9-45 years, vaccination was generally well tolerated. Because of its expected public health benefit in reducing cervical cancer and other HPV-related diseases, the vaccine has been implemented in the national vaccination programs of several countries, with over 178 million doses distributed worldwide. METHODS: Extensive efforts to assess the safety of the vaccine in routine practice have been conducted over the past 9 years since licensure, including more than 15 studies in more than 1 million preadolescents, adolescents and adults from various countries. Most have been performed in the general population although there have been some in special populations (pregnant women, HIV-infected individuals and those with systemic lupus erythematosus). RESULTS: We present a summary of the published, postlicensure safety data from active and passive surveillance. Only syncope, and possibly skin infections were associated with vaccination in the postlicensure setting. Serious adverse events, such as adverse pregnancy outcomes, autoimmune diseases (including Guillain-Barre Syndrome and multiple sclerosis), anaphylaxis, venous thromboembolism and stroke, were extensively studied, and no increase in the incidence of these events was found compared with background rates. CONCLUSIONS: These results, along with the safety data from the prelicensure clinical trials, confirm that the HPV4 vaccine has a favorable safety profile. Key policy, medical and regulatory organizations around the world have independently reviewed these data and continue to recommend routine HPV vaccination.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Vichnin, Michelle","Bonanni, Paolo","Klein, Nicola P","Garland, Suzanne M","Block, Stan L","Kjaer, Susanne K.","Sings, Heather L","Perez, Gonzalo","Haupt, Richard M","Saah, Alfred J","Lievano, Fabio","Velicer, Christine","Drury, Rosybel","Kuter, Barbara J"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-490824"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Child","Drug Related Side Effects and Adverse Reactions","Female","Human Papillomavirus Recombinant Vaccine Quadrivalent Types 6 11 16 18","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Papillomavirus Infections","Pregnancy","Product Surveillance Postmarketing","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an overview of quadrivalent human papillomavirus vaccine safety 000000002006 to 000000002015","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-490824","identifier":[{"id":"26107345","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84940052308","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a2f5065b-1a63-4c66-a6d4-676da61ad369"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Child","Drug-Related Side Effects and Adverse Reactions","Female","Human Papillomavirus Recombinant Vaccine Quadrivalent, Types 6, 11, 16, 18","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Papillomavirus Infections","Pregnancy","Product Surveillance, Postmarketing","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9F7914E19F3278B7E13D302AA032B661"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Michelle","key":"vichninpau","last":"Vichnin","name":"Vichnin, Michelle","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Paolo","key":"bonannipau","last":"Bonanni","name":"Bonanni, Paolo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nicola P","key":"kleinpau","last":"Klein","name":"Klein, Nicola P","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Suzanne M","key":"garlandpau","last":"Garland","name":"Garland, Suzanne M","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stan L","key":"blockpau","last":"Block","name":"Block, Stan L","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne K","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","name_org":"Kjaer, Susanne K","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Heather L","key":"singspau","last":"Sings","name":"Sings, Heather L","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gonzalo","key":"perezpau","last":"Perez","name":"Perez, Gonzalo","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Richard M","key":"hauptpau","last":"Haupt","name":"Haupt, Richard M","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alfred J","key":"saahpau","last":"Saah","name":"Saah, Alfred J","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Fabio","key":"lievanopau","last":"Lievano","name":"Lievano, Fabio","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christine","key":"velicerpau","last":"Velicer","name":"Velicer, Christine","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rosybel","key":"drurypau","last":"Drury","name":"Drury, Rosybel","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Barbara J","key":"kuterpau","last":"Kuter","name":"Kuter, Barbara J","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26107345"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/inf.0000000000000793","issn":["08913668","10733175"],"issn_org":["08913668"],"issue":"9","journal":"Pediatric Infectious Disease Journal","pages":"983-91","status":"p","title":"Pediatric Infectious Disease Journal","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84940052308"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a2f5065b-1a63-4c66-a6d4-676da61ad369"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An Overview of Quadrivalent Human Papillomavirus Vaccine Safety : 2006 to 2015","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-490824","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The investigational 9-valent viruslike particle vaccine against human papillomavirus (HPV) includes the HPV types in the quadrivalent HPV (qHPV) vaccine (6, 11, 16, and 18) and five additional oncogenic types (31, 33, 45, 52, and 58). Here we present the results of a study of the efficacy and immunogenicity of the 9vHPV vaccine in women 16 to 26 years of age. METHODS: We performed a randomized, international, double-blind, phase 2b-3 study of the 9vHPV vaccine in 14,215 women. Participants received the 9vHPV vaccine or the qHPV vaccine in a series of three intramuscular injections on day 1 and at months 2 and 6. Serum was collected for analysis of antibody responses. Swabs of labial, vulvar, perineal, perianal, endocervical, and ectocervical tissue were obtained and used for HPV DNA testing, and liquid-based cytologic testing (Papanicolaou testing) was performed regularly. Tissue obtained by means of biopsy or as part of definitive therapy (including a loop electrosurgical excision procedure and conization) was tested for HPV. RESULTS: The rate of high-grade cervical, vulvar, or vaginal disease irrespective of HPV type (i.e., disease caused by HPV types included in the 9vHPV vaccine and those not included) in the modified intention-to-treat population (which included participants with and those without prevalent infection or disease) was 14.0 per 1000 person-years in both vaccine groups. The rate of high-grade cervical, vulvar, or vaginal disease related to HPV-31, 33, 45, 52, and 58 in a prespecified per-protocol efficacy population (susceptible population) was 0.1 per 1000 person-years in the 9vHPV group and 1.6 per 1000 person-years in the qHPV group (efficacy of the 9vHPV vaccine, 96.7%; 95% confidence interval, 80.9 to 99.8). Antibody responses to HPV-6, 11, 16, and 18 were noninferior to those generated by the qHPV vaccine. Adverse events related to injection site were more common in the 9vHPV group than in the qHPV group. CONCLUSIONS: The 9vHPV vaccine prevented infection and disease related to HPV-31, 33, 45, 52, and 58 in a susceptible population and generated an antibody response to HPV-6, 11, 16, and 18 that was noninferior to that generated by the qHPV vaccine. The 9vHPV vaccine did not prevent infection and disease related to HPV types beyond the nine types covered by the vaccine. (Funded by Merck; ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT00543543).","author_count":27,"contributors":["Joura, Elmar A","Giuliano, Anna R","Iversen, Ole-Erik","Bouchard, Celine","Mao, Constance","Mehlsen, Jesper Løkke","Moreira, Edson D","Ngan, Yuen","Petersen, Lone Kjeld","Lazcano-Ponce, Eduardo","Pitisuttithum, Punnee","Restrepo, Jaime Alberto","Stuart, Gavin","Woelber, Linn","Yang, Yuh Cheng","Cuzick, Jack","Garland, Suzanne M","Huh, Warner","Kjaer, Susanne K","Bautista, Oliver M","Chan, Ivan S F","Chen, Joshua","Gesser, Richard","Moeller, Erin","Ritter, Michael","Vuocolo, Scott","Luxembourg, Alain"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-016450"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["Broad Spectrum HPV Vaccine Study"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Alphapapillomavirus","Antibodies Viral","Cervical Intraepithelial Neoplasia","Double Blind Method","Female","Genital Diseases Female","Humans","Incidence","Intention to Treat Analysis","Papillomavirus Infections","Papillomavirus Vaccines","Uterine Cervical Neoplasms","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a 000000000009 valent hpv vaccine against infection and intraepithelial neoplasia in women","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84923039975","version"